extraction_notes: "This is a P.C.C. in the book''s own heading on printed 98 - a Psychic Character Class - and is stored as `category: occ` with `occ_group: psychic`, because the schema has no third category and the group is what a race''s occ_restrictions matches on. The book calls it ''The Psi-Slinger O.C.C.'' four pages later, on printed 100, so the book is not consistent either. The I.S.P. formula is prose because it is an attribute expression rather than dice: M.E. x2, +10 per level. The psionic power list on printed 99 grants five named powers plus one pick per level from any category except Super, starting at level one - stored as powers_starting 1 and powers_per_level 1 with the three non-Super categories allowed. Standard Equipment stores only the catalog rows that exist; the book lists the same kit as the Gunslinger - M.D.C. body armour of choice, tinted goggles, a quality cowboy hat, riding clothes, an expensive town suit, a multi-optics band, a laser distancer, a pocket translator, a gun cleaning kit, a cigarette lighter, a pocket mirror, a silver cross, 2 pairs of handcuffs, 50 ft of rope, a two-holster gun belt, a Vibro-Blade, a Derringer, a pair of silver-plated revolvers with 60-96 silver bullets, a pair of automatic pistols, a pair of energy pistols, one more weapon of choice including a TW revolver, 1D4+4 spare E-clips each and 288 rounds per weapon, and a robot horse or a new hovercycle or land rover of choice."
