# Psi-Slinger

**Alignments.** Any, but often anarchist or evil. Those who are honourable and
live by the Code of the New West may be any alignment, including good,
unprincipled or aberrant.

The Psi-Slinger is a latent psychic with a sixth sense and the ability to power
his own weapons with nothing but psychic energy. They are much like ordinary
Gunslingers, only cockier and more flamboyant. They keep to the cities and
enter a great many shooting contests and showdowns, and between the sixth sense
and the rest of the powers they are very good at it.

Many scientists believe the Psi-Slinger is a variation or mutation of the
Burster - humans four times in five, Psi-Stalkers the rest, with the power to
create and manipulate energy. The speculation is that the psychic somehow melds
telekinesis with the manifestation of energy, but nobody knows. They appeared
only in the last decade, the first recorded case in April of 95 P.A.

They are rarer than Bursters and about as common as Mind Melters, which is what
suggests they are master psionics. For whatever reason they are most common in
the New West - perhaps mutants who arose there, perhaps drawn to the one place
the expertise pays. One persistent rumour makes them the enforcers of the
mythical Psyscape, which ninety-nine in a hundred deny, claiming not to know
where that refuge is.

Except for the powers they are fundamentally Gunslingers, with the same trade,
outlook and ethics - and are generally reckoned superior.

## Lore

Also known as the Psi-Assassin and the Energy Killer.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'psi-slinger');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'psi-slinger';

